  "note": "Debashis Pal (171 cm) keeps the repair workshop, location.nabapara.repair_workshop, every day of the week, and lives off-lane behind its front threshold (location.nabapara.pal_home, a 1680 cm authored walk from the front-door anchor, 12 minutes). The door's business hours are 08:00-12:00 and 14:00-18:30 (door.nabapara.repair_workshop_front); in both windows he is at the shop. Monday to Saturday he sleeps until 05:30, washes, cooks and eats, walks in and checks the day's jobs at the workbench (07:42), and is at the staff counter by 08:00 for collection and enquiries. The mornings alternate the counter with repair at the workbench and a tool-rack restock; he goes home for the midday meal and a rest between 12:00 and 14:00 and is back at the counter at 14:00. In the afternoon he works the finishing table, then tests at the workbench, and is back at the counter for the last hour. After closing he restocks the tool rack and walks home, cooks, eats, reads and sleeps from 23:00. On Sunday he rises at 06:30, keeps the counter for most of the day with only one restock and one bench check, and otherwise follows the same hours. Built routes are the kit's staff polylines for the 900 by 900 workshop: counter to tool rack 953 cm, to workbench 947 cm, to finishing table 1537 cm, to the door anchor 1582 cm; and three sub-paths of those same polylines: workbench to tool rack 306 cm, workbench to finishing table 590 cm, door to workbench 1399 cm. Every travel duration is ceil(sum(lengthCm)/140).",
